Audit this Node.js handler:

app.post('/profile', (req, res) => {
  db.collection('users').updateOne(
    { _id: new ObjectId(req.session.userId) },
    { $set: req.body }
  );
});

HIGH: Mass Assignment. The entire req.body is passed to $set. An attacker includes isAdmin: true.

Fix: Use an explicit allowlist:
```javascript
const ALLOWED = ['name', 'email', 'bio'];
const updates = {};
for (const key of ALLOWED) {
  if (req.body[key] !== undefined) updates[key] = req.body[key];
}
db.collection('users').updateOne(
  { _id: new ObjectId(req.session.userId) },
  { $set: updates }
);
```

Is this password hashing secure?

import hashlib
def hash_password(password):
    return hashlib.md5(password.encode()).hexdigest()

CRITICAL: Three vulnerabilities. MD5 is broken, no salt (identical passwords = identical hashes), and no timing-safe comparison.

Fix:
```python
import bcrypt
def hash_password(password):
    return bcrypt.hashpw(password.encode(), bcrypt.gensalt(rounds=12))
def verify_password(password, stored_hash):
    return bcrypt.checkpw(password.encode(), stored_hash)
```
bcrypt includes per-hash salts, is intentionally slow, and uses constant-time comparison.

Find the security bug:

app.get('/download', (req, res) => {
  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, 'files', req.query.file));
});

CRITICAL: Path Traversal. req.query.file with ../../etc/passwd reads any file.

Fix:
```javascript
const FILES_DIR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'files');
app.get('/download', (req, res) => {
  const resolved = path.resolve(FILES_DIR, req.query.file);
  if (!resolved.startsWith(FILES_DIR + path.sep)) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  res.sendFile(resolved);
});
```

Find the SSRF vulnerability:

import requests
@app.route('/fetch-url')
def fetch_url():
    url = request.args.get('url')
    return requests.get(url).text

HIGH: origin * with credentials: true is forbidden by the CORS spec. If it works, any website can make authenticated cross-origin requests.

Fix: Whitelist specific origins:
```javascript
const ALLOWED = new Set(['https://yourapp.com']);
app.use(cors({
  origin: (origin, cb) => cb(null, !origin || ALLOWED.has(origin)),
  credentials: true,
}));
```

